o range fields, no calendar/date-picker, and no clear-date control. There is no way to narrow resumes by an exact creation date or a creation-date range.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No date-period validation; invalid work/education periods accepted without feedback\", \"actual\": \"Acme Corp experience with start 2020-03: set end-date to 2019-01 (end precedes start) — accepted, no error text, no aria-invalid, no role=alert content; preview rendered \\\"Mar 2020 - Jan 2019\\\". Set end-date to 2029-12 (future; today 2026-08-27) — also accepted, input.validity.valid=true, no max attribute, preview rendered \\\"Mar 2020 - Dec 2029\\\". No rejection or feedback in either case.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Experience & education date inputs are type=\\\"month\\\". Preview renders \\\"Mar 2020 - Jun 2023\\\", \\\"Jan 2017 - Feb 2020\\\" (Mon YYYY, consistent). Checking \\\"I currently work here\\\" set end-date value=\\\"\\\" and enabled:false; preview became \\\"Mar 2020 - Present\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence across reload; all session changes are lost and deletions are reverted\", \"actual\": \"Before reload the dashboard held 5 resumes: Data Analyst Resume (created), Automation Lead Resume (duplicated+renamed, edited), QA Engineer Resume (created+edited+renamed), Product Designer Resume, Marketing Manager Resume — with Software Engineer Resume deleted. After reloading http://localhost:7005/ the dashboard shows only the 3 original seed resumes (Product Designer, Marketing Manager, Software Engineer). All created, edited, duplicated and renamed versions vanished, and the deleted \\\"Software Engineer Resume\\\" reappeared.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Dashboard rename dialog accepts a whitespace-only title, leaving the resume with an empty title; no validation feedback anywhere\", \"actual\": \"Dashboard card menu > Rename: entered \\\"   \\\" (3 spaces) and clicked Save. The dialog closed and the rename was APPLIED — the card's title is now empty (dashboard.resumes.item.yc5kslx0yrl name:\\\"\\\" where it was \\\"QA Engineer Resume (Copy)\\\"). No error, no toast, no inline message. Separately, in the editor the inline title edit rejects \\\"\\\"/\\\"   \\\" and reverts to the previous title, but likewise shows no validation feedback of any kind.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing contact fields updated preview.contact.* immediately; summary text appeared in preview.summary.text with live 67/500 counter; experience/education/skill edits appeared in preview at once; template clicks re-rendered preview instantly. No save button or reload needed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Moving Education above Experience and toggling Skills visibility both updated the preview immediately (headings reordered to EDUCATION/WORK EXPERIENCE; skills heading removed then restored). After navigating tabs, to the dashboard and back, preview heading order remained About Me, Academics, Career History, Core Competencies.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"No manual save exists; edits auto-retained across tab switches, dashboard return and reopen. Dashboard card reflected the update: title \\\"QA Engineer Resume\\\", \\\"Updated Aug 27, 2026\\\" (today) and template \\\"Modern\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Modern style: all five visible sections with content render (contact, summary, education, experience with both entries, skills). With viewport shrunk to 1280x600 the resume (docScrollH 1044 vs viewport 600) overflowed; scrolling to the bottom brought the last section (\\\"Core Competencies\\\") fully into view, so the complete resume stays readable via scrolling.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After switching across all 7 editor tabs, returning to dashboard and reopening: contact all 6 fields intact (Jane Tester / jane.tester@example.com / 555-0100 / Berlin, DE / linkedin / website), 493-char summary intact, both experience entries (Beta Labs, Acme Corp) intact, education TU Berlin intact, skills Playwright + TypeScript intact.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Copy edited (name→\\\"Jane T. Copy\\\", email→\\\"copy@example.com\\\"): original still \\\"Jane Tester\\\"/\\\"jane.tester@example.com\\\". Original then edited (location→\\\"Munich, DE\\\"): copy still shows location \\\"Berlin, DE\\\" plus its own name/email. No cross-contamination in either direction.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Renamed to \\\"QA Engineer Resume\\\"; editor.title showed \\\"QA Engineer Resume\\\" and the dashboard card displayed the same title. Reopening the resume still showed \\\"QA Engineer Resume\\\" in the editor.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Customized Summary section heading is not rendered in the Minimal style\", \"actual\": \"Section titles were customized to About Me / Career History / Academics / Core Competencies. Modern renders all four (summary=About Me); Classic renders all four (summary=ABOUT ME). Minimal renders only ACADEMICS, CAREER HISTORY, CORE COMPETENCIES — preview.summary.heading element does not exist and the preview text contains no \\\"About Me\\\", even though the Summary section is visible and its text is displayed.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
