    "content": "All 21 checklist items have been executed and recorded — coverage is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**16 PASS / 5 FAIL**\n\nThe core resume-building flows are solid: creating blank resumes, editing all content areas, switching among the three templates, section reordering/visibility, live preview, preview hide/show, duplication with full data independence, renaming, and title search with sorting all worked as specified. Live reactivity was consistently correct — no manual save exists and every edit propagated to the preview instantly.\n\n### Failures\n\n**FT-19 — Date filtering is entirely missing.** The dashboard has only 8 controls total (create, search, sort, and per-card menus). A full DOM scan including hidden elements found no date input, range fields, or date picker. This feature was never built.\n\n**CS-11 — No persistence.** All state is in-memory only. After reloading, the 5-resume dashboard reverted to the 3 original seeds: every created, edited, duplicated, and renamed version vanished, and the deleted resume reappeared.\n\n**CS-9 — No date-period validation.** An end date preceding the start (`2019-01` against start `2020-03`) and a future end date (`2029-12`, today being 2026-08-27) were both accepted silently and rendered in the preview as \"Mar 2020 - Jan 2019\" and \"Mar 2020 - Dec 2029\". No error text, no `aria-invalid`, no `max` attribute.\n\n**CS-21 — Whitespace title actually saves.** This is the most severe defect found. The two rename paths behave inconsistently: the editor's inline title edit correctly rejects empty/whitespace input, but the *dashboard rename dialog* accepts `\"   \"` and applies it, leaving the resume with a completely empty title on its card. Neither path shows any validation feedback (no alert, toast, or inline message).\n\n**CT-20 — Custom heading dropped in Minimal.** The customized Summary heading (\"About Me\") renders in Modern and Classic, but the Minimal template omits `preview.summary.heading` entirely while still displaying the summary text — so the user's customization is silently discarded in that one style.\n\n### Note on test-order interaction\nCS-21's whitespace rename left a resume with an empty title mid-session. I restored it to a valid title (\"Automation Lead Resume\") before continuing, so subsequent search/sort/duplication results were unaffected by that defect."
  }
